export anchor PunchCardStyle:
    number: 166
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Punch card
    idea: Every panel is an 80-column punch card on manila stock, and the data is literally punched, so summary digits, finished tasks and daily counts appear as dark rectangular holes beside printed column numbers.
    base: light
    palette:
        desk: #e4e9ef, the page behind the deck
        manilaStock: #f3e7c6, every card
        paleStock: #f7eedb, alternate cards, status boxes and rows
        printBrown: #6a4a22, printed labels, digits and field lines
        rule: #b49a6a, unpunched slots and hairlines, never text
        typedInk: #1d1a14, interpreted text and the primary button
        hole: #2b3440, punched holes as data
        tabBlue: #cfdcea, deck divider tabs
        green: #1f5c34, the On track ring
        amber: #85480a, the At risk triangle
        red: #8f1f1f, the Behind oblong and the Overdue diamond
        focus: #1b4fae, the focus outline
    type:
        Typed text uses Courier New, Nimbus Mono PS, Courier, monospace.
        Printed labels use Arial Narrow, Helvetica Neue Condensed, Roboto
        Condensed, Liberation Sans Narrow, Arial in bold caps. Total
        figures are 48px bold mono, the greeting 30px bold caps, card
        titles 17px bold caps, body 14 to 15px, labels 11px narrow caps
        tracked 0.08em and printed digits 9px narrow.
    layout:
        Every block is a card with its top-left corner clipped at 45
        degrees. The header card has the spaced brand with a job card
        caption, a Keypunch search field over faint column ticks, a black
        Punch new project button, a bell and the operator name. Under it a
        row of blue deck divider tabs is the nav, with Home in manila and
        raised. The greeting card shows the greeting, date and a dashed red
        overdue box. The summary card splits into four fields by brown
        column lines, each with a column range label, the big typed figure
        and a printed 0 to 9 grid where each digit of the figure is punched
        out. Below, a wide column is the project deck, one card each, with
        sequence number, name, department and due date typed on top, a row
        of slots punched one per finished task, a status box at right and
        printed column numbers 1 to 80 along the bottom. The narrow column
        holds the chart card, 14 columns of 17 slots punched from the
        bottom, and a stack of thin activity strips with BW sequence
        numbers. Below 960px the columns stack.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 10px between cards, 16 to 24px between sections, a 32px left inset that clears the clipped corner.
    density: Dense and data-literal, with rows of tiny slots and printed digits and one big typed number per field.
    corners: A 22px clipped top-left corner on large cards and 14px on strips, 6px rounding elsewhere, tabs rounded 8px on top.
    borders: 2px brown field dividers, a 1px rule above the column numbers, outlined unpunched slots, 2px currentColor status boxes.
    shadows: Only a 1px brown edge under each card, like stacked stock.
    icons:
        Hole shapes beside caps words. A ring for On track, a solid
        triangle for At risk, a solid oblong for Behind and a diamond with
        a bang for Overdue.
    focus: A 3px focus blue outline offset 3px.
    tone: Data-processing jargon, such as Keypunch, Operator, Punch new project and Project deck.
